#show: worksheet.with(
  title: [Past Tense Verbs],
  subject: [English],
  grade: [Grade 4],
  instructions: [Read each question carefully. Write your answers neatly.],
)

#callout(kind: "remember")[
  A *past tense verb* tells us about something that already happened. Most verbs add _-ed_: walk → walk*ed*. Some verbs change completely: go → *went*.
]

= Part A: Fill in the blanks

#question(points: 4)[
  Write the past tense of the verb in brackets.
  + Yesterday, I #blank(answer: [walked]) to school. (walk)
  + She #blank(answer: [played]) with her friends after lunch. (play)
  + We #blank(answer: [ate]) pizza for dinner last night. (eat)
  + The dog #blank(answer: [ran]) across the garden. (run)
]

#question(points: 2)[
  Choose the correct sentence.
  #mcq(
    [He goed to the park.],
    [He went to the park.],
    [He gone to the park.],
    answer: 2,
  )
]

#question(points: 2)[
  #true-false(answer: true)[The past tense of _jump_ is _jumped_.]
  #true-false(answer: false)[The past tense of _see_ is _seed_.]
]

= Part B: Matching

#question(points: 5)[
  Match each present tense verb with its past tense.
  #matching(
    ([go], [went]),
    ([swim], [swam]),
    ([write], [wrote]),
    ([bring], [brought]),
    ([drink], [drank]),
  )
]

= Part C: Writing

#question(points: 5)[
  Write 3 to 4 sentences about what you did last weekend. Use at least *three* past tense verbs. Underline each past tense verb you use.
  #answer-lines(count: 5, answer: [Sample answer: On Saturday I visited my grandmother. We cooked soup and played cards. Then I helped her in the garden.])
  #answer[Award 1 point for each correct past tense verb (up to 3), 1 point for complete sentences with capital letters and full stops, and 1 point for the topic being about last weekend.]
]

